    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0097" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg77"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 456.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you herewith a
                    translation of a communication from Count Manderstrom, minister of foreign
                    affairs for the United Kingdom of Sweden and Norway, to Mr. Haldeman, United
                    States minister at that court.</p>
                <p>This communication expressly denies the allegation made by Mr. Arman to M. Drouyn
                    de l’Huys that a contract had been entered into between him and the government
                    of Sweden for the sale of certain of the rebel vessels building at Bordeaux.</p>
                <p>I have just enclosed a copy of this communication, together with a copy of Mr.
                    Haldeman’s letter to me accompanying it, to M. Drouyn de l’Huys.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d99-a1.xml" xpointer="d99-a1"/>
            </div>
